Package: corvusjsonschema
Title: A High-Performance 'JSON Schema' Validator
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Matthew", "Adams", email = "matthew.adams@endjin.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Endjin Limited", role = c("cph", "fnd")))
Description: Validates R values and 'JSON' text against 'JSON Schema' drafts 4, 6,
    7, 2019-09 and 2020-12, with results collection and annotations. A schema is
    compiled once into a validator, which reads R lists and vectors in place, or
    parses 'JSON' text itself. The evaluator is the 'corvus-json-schema' 'Rust'
    crate, which passes the whole 'JSON-Schema-Test-Suite'.
License: Apache License (>= 2)
URL: https://github.com/corvus-dotnet/Corvus.JsonSchema
BugReports: https://github.com/corvus-dotnet/Corvus.JsonSchema/issues
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Suggests: jsonlite
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc (>= 1.89)
Encoding: UTF-8
NeedsCompilation: yes
